    "The cart's 'Goes well with' map (categories.complement_category_ids, siruk-web fff688a3, 2026-10-09).",
    "Applied by scripts/set-complements.py, keyed by category path so it survives an id change.",
    "How the cart uses it (CartRecommendationService): for each cart product, the lists of its categories AND their ancestors are merged and expanded to subcategories; products from them rank after real bought-together pairs and before the automatic fallback (same pet, categories not in the cart). Only the cart's own pet trees are searched, so a cross-pet target is useless. At most 8 cards, 2 per brand, in stock only.",
    "Rules used: set on LEAVES (a list on a parent is inherited by every leaf under it — a vet diet must not inherit 'treats' from Dog > Food); 2–3 targets each, the most likely add-on first; a vet-diet / pharmacy category never points at treats; food points at the other food form (mixed feeding) plus the add-on a food buyer needs (treats, bowls, litter for cats).",
    "Drafted 2026-10-12 for the PM to review — the PM can edit any row in the admin (Category → 'Goes well with categories')."
